00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.120 align:start position:0%
of all the effects of the economic  crisis in Europe the one real scourge is  a youth unemployment some 5.6 million  young people aged between 15 and 24 were  jobless in the European Union in  September the unemployment rate for them  is more than twice that for adults in  Croatia Greece and Spain half of young  people are out of work that's why  European leaders have been taking  extraordinary steps to address this  urgent problem as demonstrated by the  recent Paris conference on youth  employment four main measures are being  taken to get young people out of  Europe's jobless queues the first is the  youth guarantee scheme aimed at ensuring  that all people under 25 receive a  quality offer of employment further  education or a traineeship within four  months of leaving school second the  youth employment initiative allows  funding from a 6 million euro total  budget for young people in regions where  jobless rates are more than twenty-five  percent third quality traineeships aimed  at easing the transition from education  to full-time employment and also an  effort to change public attitudes toward  apprenticeship style learning finally  encouraging young people to look for  work across Europe's borders in  neighboring states through labour  mobility programs like the US job  initiative the portal links uses to more  than 1.4 million job vacancies and over  300,000 registered employers these  measures are all part of Europe's  comprehensive program to tackle this  number one priority
 

